    <DataNode elementId="AT3G47340-MONOMER" textLabel="Asparagine synthetase [glutamine-hydrolyzing] 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G47340-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">There are three genes in Arabidopsis encoding asparagine synthetase (AS). ASN1 and ASN2 are the predominantly expressed genes, and they are mainly detected in the shoots. The two genes are regulated by light, carbon and nitrogen status of the cell, but in an opposite fashion. ASN1 is repressed by light and sucrose, whereas ASN2 is induced under the same conditions. For ASN1, the addition of nitrogen-transporting amino acids can partially relieve the sucrose repression of its expression. In contrast, the sucrose induction of ASN2 is partially repressed by the addition of these amino acids. ASN1 is indicated to be involved in asparagine synthesis in the dark, for nitrogen storage and transport. ASN2 is predicted to be involved in asparagine synthesis in the light, for protein biosynthesis, or for ammonia detoxification under ammonia rich conditions. The activities of ASN1, ASN2 and ASN3 were demonstrated by functional complementation of a yeast asparagine auxotrophic mutant. None of them has been characterized for kinetic properties.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G47340-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Glutamine-dependent asparagine synthetase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="DARK INDUCIBLE 6" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-7241" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G47340.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G47340" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_9881155" />
    </DataNode>
